  "notes": "Web 386 — CONNECT-SEARCH-COLLAPSE-NOV8: searching Connect members no longer collapses the page. Convicted in Asjad's hands Nov 8 (screen recording, Connect > Find people): tapping the 'Name or business' field opened the keyboard, and within a second or two the keyboard was dismissed, the field stood empty and unfocused, and the page snapped — twice in 13 seconds; the search was unusable. The mechanism: CL.reconcile could never converge for a pair whose directory identity had moved since its request doc froze — each pass flipped the entry snapshot->directory and reported changed, so Connect's refreshLive repainted the whole screen every few seconds forever, and every repaint rebuilt the search box empty and unfocused. The fix, two seams: (1) js/connectlive.js — reconcile is judged by its NET effect: con_list is snapshotted before the pass and compared after; a tug-of-war pass that nets to the list it started with resolves false, while a real landing still resolves true. No leg's writes changed — the directory remains the peer's current word. (2) modules/connect.js — the search box is defended: its text lives in module state (uiQuery), is painted back as the input's value on every render, and the rerender funnel returns focus to the successor box with the caret at the end. Proof on these ship bytes: tools/connect-search-collapse-nov8-test.js 29/29; the connect family re-run at its recorded baselines, zero regressions. Job A, the route benches and all other parked work NOT in this commit. version stays 63.",
